  "limitations": [
    "Fixed subset, not full official test benchmark.",
    "Third-person TV video differs from glasses footage.",
    "Adjacent frames and tracks may correlate; no independent-subject confidence claim.",
    "Checkpoint was trained on the training portion of VSGaze including VAT; evaluation uses only original official test-show labels.",
    "Conditional accuracy/distance exclude unmatched heads; joint success includes missing heads as failures.",
    "Only annotated people are scored; unannotated detected people cannot be counted as false positives.",
    "No threshold tuning, model updates, or test-driven resolution selection.",
    "Peak L2 is measured for matched ground-truth in-frame cases even if predicted out; joint success also requires predicted in-frame.",
    "Normalized L2 uses x/image-width and y/image-height, not pixels, degrees or fraction of diagonal.",
    "Raw annotation boxes are unsmoothed; matching differs from official ground-truth-box model evaluation.",
    "Frames are sparse accuracy samples, not an 8 fps playback or live throughput trial."
  ]
